# CODEOWNERS for idfkit-developers, the unified documentation site.
#
# WHY THE WHOLE REPOSITORY, AND NOT A LIST OF PATHS.
#
# In the Python library this file named owners for `docs/`, `mkdocs.yml` and
# `.github/workflows/docs.yml` specifically, because those were islands of shared
# material inside a repository that otherwise belonged to one language. Here there
# is no such distinction to draw: every file in this repository is the site or is
# tooling that acts on the site, so the entry is the repository (001-FR-057,
# 003-FR-004).
#
# 001-FR-091: the rule has no override. An unavailable reviewer blocks the merge.
# Do not add a bypass, do not grant an exemption, and do not merge on the grounds
# that the reviewer sets currently overlap. They overlap today, which is what makes
# the rule cheap to obey now and is precisely why it is written down before they
# diverge.
#
# The team slugs below must exist in the "idfkit" GitHub organisation and must have
# write access to this repository, otherwise GitHub silently ignores the entry and
# the rule does not bind. Pair this file with a branch protection rule on the
# default branch that requires review from Code Owners.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE POINT OF THE MOVE. While the site lived inside the Python
# library, a maintainer of the JavaScript library could be named here and still not
# merge, because merging needs write access to the repository the file sits in.
# Standing to review and standing to merge are different things, and only one of
# them could be granted by a CODEOWNERS line. Here both maintainer teams hold the
# same standing over the same repository, which is a property of where the site
# lives rather than of what this file says.
#
# Matching follows GitHub's rules: the last matching pattern wins, so keep the most
# specific entries at the bottom.

# Everything. The site, its build, its checks, its scripts.
*                                       @idfkit/python-maintainers @idfkit/javascript-maintainers

# This file itself, so the review rule cannot be relaxed without the same review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @idfkit/python-maintainers @idfkit/javascript-maintainers
